<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51641" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάδος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], ὁ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>jar</i> or <i>vessel for water</i> or
			<i>wine</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				534.3
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				549
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἀντλητικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CPR</u>
					232.12
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; said to be 
				Ion.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεράμιον</span>,
			Clitarch.Gloss. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.473b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a liquid
			measure,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφορεύς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
				155a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>2 Ch.</u>
					2.10(9)
				</span></i>
			 (cod. A), cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				155.4
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Hermes</u>
				64.274
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίνει τετραχόοισι κάδοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hedyl.
				</span></i>
			 ap. Ath.l.c.; later, <i>half an</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφ.</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Script. Metrol.</u>
				1.257
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.144
			</span></i> Hultsch. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καδίσκος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1032
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>funerary urn,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Jahresh.
				8.154
			</span></i>.—The metre usu. requires <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάδος</span>, never <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάδδος</span>
			which is written in <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>in Ph.</u>
				268.2
			</span></i>, al.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάδδιχος</span>.</div>
